      "reason": "R5 (in-space thin-film PV manufacturing) is uniquely leveraged and unclaimed: no funded program makes PV in space (OSAM-1 cancelled ~$2B, OSAM-2 concluded, heritage is polymer printing/ZBLAN/ceramic), mass leverage vs SOTA arrays is ~100x, and perovskite/CIGS-on-polymer resilience is demonstrated. Critical open path: deposition process demo at rate and quality on orbit (WSF MBE precedent is 30 years old and made no device); AO limits LEO membranes; economics face Starship launch-cost and Starlink COTS-silicon pressure.",
